The new diff adds _timestamped_record_name that requires stamp[8] == '-' and stamp[:8].isdigit() and stamp[9:15].isdigit(). If a record directory contains a JSON file named codereview-2026-11-04-031306.json (valid ISO format with dash separators), stamp[8] is '0' (not '-'), so the function returns False and falls back to mtime ordering. This could incorrectly prefer an older record over a newer one if both lack the exact dash-at-position-8 pattern.